Statement of Purpose

The laws of most jurisdictions throughout the world automatically confer
exclusive Copyright and Related Rights (defined below) upon the creator
and subsequent owner(s) (each and all, an "owner") of an original work of
authorship and/or a database (each, a "work").

Certain owners wish to relinquish all of those rights to a work, whether
for the benefit of the public domain or because they consider it
undesirable to retain certain copyright and related rights in a work.

This document is a Creative Commons Copyright Waiver (the "waiver") that
may be used by such owners to affirmatively dedicate any and all copyright
and related rights in a work to the public domain, to the extent that such
dedication is permitted by applicable law.

The waiver is made for the benefit of the public at large and to the
detriment of the owner's heirs and successors.  The waiver is intended
to relinquish all of the owner's present and future rights under
copyright law, whether arising from a work or otherwise, whether they are
now known or hereafter conjectured to exist.

Copyright and Related Rights. A work made available under this
waiver may be copied, modified, distributed and performed, even for
commercial purposes, all without asking permission.  These rights include,
but are not limited to, the right to reproduce the work in copies, to
prepare derivative works based upon the work, to distribute copies of the
work, to publicly display the work, to publicly perform the work, to
publicly perform the work by means of a digital audio transmission, and to
otherwise make use of the work in any way that is not otherwise prohibited
by applicable law.

The person who associated a work with this waiver has made an affirmation
that the owner has, to the best of the owner's knowledge, made a
reasonable effort to ascertain that no applicable law prohibits the
dedication of all of the copyright and related rights in the work to the
public domain, and that there are no legal proceedings pending or
threatened that could impair the owner's ability to make such a
dedication.

This waiver does not provide any permission to use any trademarks, service
marks, trade names, logos or corporate insignia that are associated with a
work unless such permission is expressly given in conjunction with this
waiver.

By using this waiver, the owner relinquishes all rights to the work,
including but not limited to:

* The right to reproduce the work in copies;
* The right to prepare derivative works based upon the work;
* The right to distribute copies of the work;
* The right to publicly display the work;
* The right to publicly perform the work;
* The right to publicly perform the work by means of a digital audio
  transmission;
* The right to make translations of the work;
* The right to make adaptations of the work;
* The right to make other alterations to the work;
* The right to exploit the work commercially;
* The right to otherwise use the work in any way.

The waiver is applicable worldwide and is to be interpreted according to
the substantive law of the jurisdiction where the waiver is asserted.

No Warranties

The waiver is provided as-is and without warranty of any kind, either
express or implied, including, without limitation, the implied warranties
of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose and non-infringement.
In no event shall the lawful holder of this waiver be liable for any
direct, indirect, special, incidental or consequential damages arising out
of the use or inability to use this waiver.

By using this waiver, you accept and agree that the work is dedicated to
the public domain to the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, and
that no copyright or related rights remain in the work.